    {
      "CVE": "CVE-2026-79603",
      "Description": "x86 PV guests can free memory pages while still keeping a stale TLB entry\npointing to them.  A TLB flush is only issued by Xen (if needed) when the\npage is re-used.  Since it's possible for the page to be scrubbed ahead of\nthe TLB flush, there's a window where a PV guest can modify an already\nscrubbed page.",
      "Threats": [
        {
          "Type": "Impact",
          "Severity": "moderate"
        }
